ead_before": -9.91, "lead_after": -9.96, "points_lost": 0.05, "best": "B9"}, {"turn": 78, "color": "W", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -9.96, "lead_after": -9.97, "points_lost": -0.01, "best": "pass"}, {"turn": 79, "color": "B", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -9.97, "lead_after": -10.0, "points_lost": 0.03, "best": "B9"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Trading Blows Across Row Six", "summary": "The 12k won as White by 10 points. Opus 5.5 trailed from the opening, dropping to -9.2 by move 13, and a long middle game of mutual blunders never closed the gap. Opus 5.5 lost 17 points or more three times, and the 12k handed nearly all of it back each time, so the final lead of -10.0 looks much like the lead from move 13.", "moments": [{"turn": 13, "text": "Black H4 lost 4.4 points, taking the lead from -4.8 to -9.2. The engine wanted G6. It was the first real slide, and Opus 5.5 spent the rest of the game chasing it."}, {"turn": 16, "text": "After Black B5 lost 3.3 points and left the lead at -12.5, White B6 gave back 8.2 as the engine's C5 went unplayed. The lead moved to -4.3, Opus 5.5's best position since the opening, and it stayed within reach."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "Black G8 lost 17.7 points, dropping the lead from -12.0 to -29.7. The engine preferred E3, on the open lower side, over pushing into the top right against White's row-six wall. It is the first of three huge swings in this stretch."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "White F7 lost 17.8 points, moving the lead from -29.6 back to -11.9, after Black J7 had lost 17.8 itself. The engine's choice was C3 both times. The 12k handed back every point Opus 5.5 had just given away."}, {"turn": 37, "text": "Black D8 lost 11.8 points, taking the lead from -21.8 to -33.6, the worst position of the game. White F9 returned 11.7 and the lead went back to -21.9. The same trade repeated at moves 39–42, with the engine pointing at E3 and C3 down below each time."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and compute groups, liberties and area counts of the current position, and the other commands just cat or append to games.md; none of it tries candidate moves or looks ahead.", "stop": false}}